  "headnote_district_ruling": "Judge Chesler dismissed claims alleging that BASF and its lawyers had concealed and destroyed evidence that talc products contained asbestos, causing earlier personal-injury claimants to abandon, dismiss, or settle their cases.",
  "qualification_rationale": "The case became a substantial Third Circuit authority on fraud, fraudulent concealment, the New Jersey litigation privilege, spoliation injury, Rooker-Feldman, and the limits of prospective relief aimed at prior state litigation.",
  "appellate_posture_note": "The Third Circuit reversed dismissal of the fraud and fraudulent-concealment claims, affirmed dismissal of the New Jersey RICO claim, and rejected relief directed at hypothetical future state proceedings.",
